---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="FAQs ✦ Dosezy Frequently Asked Questions">
	<Header />
	<main class="flex-grow pt-28 sm:pt-32 pb-16 bg-[#030407] bg-grid-pattern">
		<div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
			
			<!-- Hero Header -->
			<div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-16">
				<span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-mono font-semibold bg-sky-500/10 text-sky-300 border border-sky-500/20">
					FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS (v2.3.1)
				</span>
				<h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl sm:text-6xl font-extrabold text-white font-display">
					Frequently Asked Questions
				</h1>
				<p class="mt-4 text-neutral-400 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed">
					Find simple, friendly answers about Dosezy features, pill reminders, stock tracking, adherence analytics, offline privacy, and family profile management.
				</p>
			</div>

			<!-- Live Search Input -->
			<div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-14">
				<div class="relative">
					<input 
						type="text" 
						id="faq-search" 
						placeholder="Search questions (e.g. stock refill, grouped alarms, analytics, languages, offline privacy, late colors)..." 
						class="w-full px-5 py-4 rounded-2xl bg-[#0a0c10] border border-white/10 text-white placeholder-neutral-500 focus:outline-none focus:border-sky-500/50 text-sm shadow-xl"
					/>
					<svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 absolute right-4 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
						<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M21 21l-6-6m2-5a7 7 0 11-14 0 7 7 0 0114 0z" />
					</svg>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- FAQ Accordion List -->
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-4" id="faq-list">
				
				<!-- Question 1: What is Dosezy -->
				<details class="faq-item vercel-card rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-[#0a0c10]/95 group overflow-hidden" open>
					<summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-white text-base hover:text-sky-300 transition-colors list-none">
						<span>What is Dosezy?</span>
						<svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
							<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
						</svg>
					</summary>
					<div class="px-6 pb-6 text-xs text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed border-t border-white/5 pt-4">
						Dosezy is a simple, friendly, and smart medication reminder app. It helps you, your family members, and caregivers manage daily medicines, set alarms, track pill inventory, monitor adherence progress, and ensure no dose is ever missed.
					</div>
				</details>

				<!-- Question 2: Account & Offline -->
				<details class="faq-item vercel-card rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-[#0a0c10]/95 group overflow-hidden">
					<summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-white text-base hover:text-sky-300 transition-colors list-none">
						<span>Do I need to create an account or have internet?</span>
						<svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
							<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
						</svg>
					</summary>
					<div class="px-6 pb-6 text-xs text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed border-t border-white/5 pt-4">
						No! Dosezy is 100% local-first and offline. You do not need to register, log in, or have an internet connection. All your health data and reminders stay safely stored directly on your phone in an offline database.
					</div>
				</details>

				<!-- Question 3: Grouped Alarms -->
				<details class="faq-item vercel-card rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-[#0a0c10]/95 group overflow-hidden">
					<summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-white text-base hover:text-sky-300 transition-colors list-none">
						<span>What happens if I take multiple medicines at the same time?</span>
						<svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
							<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
						</svg>
					</summary>
					<div class="px-6 pb-6 text-xs text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed border-t border-white/5 pt-4 space-y-2">
						<p>Dosezy automatically combines all medicines scheduled for the exact same minute (e.g. 8:00 AM) into a single grouped alarm screen.</p>
						<p>You get an interactive checklist of your medicines with medicine photos, meal instructions, and a prominent green <strong>"Take All"</strong> button along with an orange <strong>"Snooze (10 min)"</strong> button, preventing overlapping alarms.</p>
					</div>
				</details>

				<!-- Question 4: Stock Tracking -->
				<details class="faq-item vercel-card rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-[#0a0c10]/95 group overflow-hidden">
					<summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-white text-base hover:text-sky-300 transition-colors list-none">
						<span>How does pill stock and refill tracking work?</span>
						<svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
							<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
						</svg>
					</summary>
					<div class="px-6 pb-6 text-xs text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed border-t border-white/5 pt-4 space-y-2">
						<p>When adding or editing a medicine, you can enter your current tablet count (e.g. 60) and your low-stock alert threshold (e.g. 10).</p>
						<p>Every time you mark a dose as "Taken", Dosezy automatically subtracts the dose amount from your stock and displays an orange <strong>⚠️ Refill Warning</strong> badge whenever it is time to reorder.</p>
					</div>
				</details>

				<!-- Question 5: Supported Languages -->
				<details class="faq-item vercel-card rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-[#0a0c10]/95 group overflow-hidden">
					<summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-white text-base hover:text-sky-300 transition-colors list-none">
						<span>Does Dosezy support my native language?</span>
						<svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
							<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
						</svg>
					</summary>
					<div class="px-6 pb-6 text-xs text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed border-t border-white/5 pt-4 space-y-2">
						<p>Yes! Dosezy features complete native translations in 12 major languages:</p>
						<p class="font-mono text-[11px] text-sky-300">English, Spanish, Hindi, Chinese, Portuguese, Arabic, French, German, Japanese, Russian, Italian, and Bengali.</p>
						<p>The app automatically detects your phone's system language, and you can change it anytime in <strong>Menu > Preferences</strong>.</p>
					</div>
				</details>

				<!-- Question 6: Status Colors -->
				<details class="faq-item vercel-card rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-[#0a0c10]/95 group overflow-hidden">
					<summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-white text-base hover:text-sky-300 transition-colors list-none">
						<span>How do dose status colors work on the Home screen?</span>
						<svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
							<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
						</svg>
					</summary>
					<div class="px-6 pb-6 text-xs text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed border-t border-white/5 pt-4 space-y-2">
						<p><strong class="text-emerald-400">Green:</strong> Dose confirmed as Taken (shows completion time).</p>
						<p><strong class="text-white">Normal Text:</strong> Dose is upcoming or due recently (within your customizable Late Window).</p>
						<p><strong class="text-amber-400">Orange:</strong> Dose is Late (3 to 6 hours past due by default). An orange "Mark Late" action appears.</p>
						<p><strong class="text-red-400">Red:</strong> Dose is Missed (more than 6 hours past due by default).</p>
					</div>
				</details>

				<!-- Question 7: Analytics -->
				<details class="faq-item vercel-card rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-[#0a0c10]/95 group overflow-hidden">
					<summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-white text-base hover:text-sky-300 transition-colors list-none">
						<span>Where can I see my adherence percentage and dose history?</span>
						<svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
							<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
						</svg>
					</summary>
					<div class="px-6 pb-6 text-xs text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed border-t border-white/5 pt-4 space-y-2">
						<p>Go to <strong>Menu > Analytics</strong> to view your total adherence percentage ring score across <strong>Week</strong>, <strong>Month</strong>, <strong>Year</strong>, and <strong>All Time</strong>.</p>
						<p>You can also tap the <strong>Schedule</strong> tab to see colored adherence dot markers for every day on the calendar.</p>
					</div>
				</details>

				<!-- Question 8: Emergency Services -->
				<details class="faq-item vercel-card rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-[#0a0c10]/95 group overflow-hidden">
					<summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-white text-base hover:text-sky-300 transition-colors list-none">
						<span>How do I call emergency services or personal contacts in an emergency?</span>
						<svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
							<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
						</svg>
					</summary>
					<div class="px-6 pb-6 text-xs text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed border-t border-white/5 pt-4 space-y-2">
						<p>Go to <strong>Menu > Emergency Contacts</strong>:</p>
						<ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-neutral-300">
							<li><strong>Official Public Helplines:</strong> Dosezy automatically detects your region (India, USA/Canada, UK, EU, China, Japan, Russia, Brazil, Bangladesh, Australia) with 1-tap dialing for ambulance, police, fire, or universal emergency lines.</li>
							<li><strong>Personal Emergency Contacts:</strong> You can save custom numbers for your family doctor, partner, or caregiver with the <strong>"+ Add Emergency Contact"</strong> button.</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</details>

				<!-- Question 9: Doctor Reports -->
				<details class="faq-item vercel-card rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-[#0a0c10]/95 group overflow-hidden">
					<summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-white text-base hover:text-sky-300 transition-colors list-none">
						<span>How do I export my data for doctor visits?</span>
						<svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
							<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
						</svg>
					</summary>
					<div class="px-6 pb-6 text-xs text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed border-t border-white/5 pt-4">
						Go to <strong>Menu > Export Data</strong> and choose <strong>PDF Report</strong> to generate a clean, printable medical report with current prescriptions, timings, food instructions, and adherence logs formatted for your doctor. You can also export full JSON or CSV backup archives.
					</div>
				</details>

				<!-- Question 10: Caregiver / Cloud Roadmap -->
				<details class="faq-item vercel-card rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-[#0a0c10]/95 group overflow-hidden">
					<summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-white text-base hover:text-sky-300 transition-colors list-none">
						<span>Is multi-device sync or caregiver web sharing available?</span>
						<svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
							<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
						</svg>
					</summary>
					<div class="px-6 pb-6 text-xs text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed border-t border-white/5 pt-4 space-y-2">
						<p>In the current version, Dosezy is built to be <strong>100% offline and private</strong> by default.</p>
						<p>An optional, self-hostable sync server and a dedicated Caregiver Web Portal are planned for the upcoming <strong>v3.0–v3.9 product roadmap</strong>. Offline use will always remain fully supported and free.</p>
					</div>
				</details>

			</div>

		</div>
	</main>
	<Footer />
</Layout>

<script>
	const faqSearch = document.getElementById('faq-search') as HTMLInputElement;
	const faqItems = document.querySelectorAll('.faq-item');

	if (faqSearch) {
		faqSearch.addEventListener('input', (e) => {
			const query = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).value.toLowerCase();
			faqItems.forEach(item => {
				const text = item.textContent?.toLowerCase() || '';
				const match = text.includes(query);
				(item as HTMLElement).style.display = match ? 'block' : 'none';
			});
		});
	}
</script>
